    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**One file, one function** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.service`:\n\nThe `customerCode` now builds as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n- `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` \u2014 a per-city 4-digit sequence, one more than the owners already in that city (filtered from `findAll()`, case-insensitively by city)\n\nI extracted a tiny private `prefix(...)` helper so the two three-letter prefixes reuse the same logic rather than growing the method.\n\n## Why nothing else needed touching\n\nThe membership number is derived, not stored \u2014 `OwnerMapper` computes it as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + ...`. Because it reads `getCustomerCode()` at mapping time, it automatically rebuilds on the new format the moment `customerCode` changes. No mapper, model, or repository edit was required, keeping the structural impact to a single small, low-complexity function in one file.\n\nFull suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass (including the new `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` shape).",
